<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:spiffworkflow="http://spiffworkflow.org/bpmn/schema/1.0/core" id="Definitions_OrchestratorAgent" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn">
  <bpmn:process id="orchestrator_agent" name="Orchestrator Agent" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:documentation>The agent the Software Development process hands a Work Item to when `orchestrator` is ticked instead of assigning it to a person. It reads the brief off the Work Item, decides which specialist can build the thing, and delegates over A2A — each specialist is a shape in the Tools sub-process, so widening the roster is a shape, not a code change. It runs as a sub-process of the caller, so the Work Item is already the instance context and the report goes back as workflow data.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="start" name="Orchestration requested">
      <bpmn:documentation>Started by the Call Activity in the Software Development process when a Work Item has `orchestrator` ticked. Deliberately a plain start event: a called process is started by its caller, so it carries no trigger of its own.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f1" sourceRef="start" targetRef="read_brief" />
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="read_brief" name="Read the work item" spiffworkflow:serverScript="Orchestrator Agent: Read the Work Item" spiffworkflow:scriptType="Server Script" spiffworkflow:scriptName="Orchestrator Agent: Read the Work Item">
      <bpmn:documentation>Builds the agent's brief from the Work Item that is this instance's context — the same title and description a person would have read.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>f1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f2" sourceRef="read_brief" targetRef="orchestrate" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="orchestrate" name="Decide and delegate" spiffworkflow:serviceType="ai_agent" spiffworkflow:aiBackend="direct_api" spiffworkflow:aiProvider="Anthropic" spiffworkflow:aiModel="claude-sonnet-5" spiffworkflow:aiOutputVariable="ai_result" spiffworkflow:aiSystemPrompt="You are the Orchestrator. The Software Development process hands you a work item that was flagged for you instead of being assigned to a person, and you are responsible for getting it built.&#10;&#10;You do not build anything yourself. You have specialist agents as tools, one per kind of work, and your job is to read the brief, decide which specialist can do it, and hand them a clear instruction.&#10;&#10;Work in this order.&#10;&#10;1. Read the work item brief and decide what actually has to be built.&#10;2. If one of your specialist tools covers it, call that tool with a self-contained instruction. The specialist cannot see the work item or this conversation, so the instruction must carry everything it needs — what to build, against which system, and any URL or identifier named in the brief.&#10;3. If nothing you have covers it, do not guess and do not call a tool. Say plainly what the work item needs and that no specialist is available for it.&#10;&#10;A specialist may take a while, and it may come back reporting that it stopped short. Report what it actually said — never claim work was completed that the specialist did not confirm.&#10;&#10;Finish with a short plain-language report: what you decided, who you delegated to, and what came back. No preamble, no bullet points, no invented next steps." spiffworkflow:aiUserPrompt="{{ work_item_brief }}" spiffworkflow:aiResponseFormat="text" spiffworkflow:aiMaxTokens="0" spiffworkflow:aiTimeout="120" spiffworkflow:aiMaxRetries="2" spiffworkflow:aiAgentConfig="Orchestrator Agent" spiffworkflow:aiToolsAdhoc="orchestrator_tools" spiffworkflow:aiMaxToolCalls="8">
      <bpmn:documentation>Chooses a specialist and delegates to it over A2A. The tools are the shapes of the Tools sub-process below.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>f2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f3" sourceRef="orchestrate" targetRef="answer" />
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="answer" name="Record the outcome" spiffworkflow:serverScript="Orchestrator Agent: Record the Outcome" spiffworkflow:scriptType="Server Script" spiffworkflow:scriptName="Orchestrator Agent: Record the Outcome">
      <bpmn:documentation>Hands the report back to the caller as workflow data and records it on the Work Item. Deliberately writes no Work Item field — status belongs to the Software Development process.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>f3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f4" sourceRef="answer" targetRef="end" />
    <bpmn:endEvent id="end" name="Orchestrated">
      <bpmn:incoming>f4</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:adHocSubProcess id="orchestrator_tools" name="Tools (A2A specialists)">
      <bpmn:documentation>The specialists the orchestrator may delegate to. Referenced as its toolbox, so it is not wired into the sequence flow. One shape per specialist — adding another is a shape plus a tick of "Exposed over A2A" on that agent.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="delegate_connector_agent" name="A2A &#8594; Connector Agent" spiffworkflow:serviceType="connector" spiffworkflow:connectorId="a2a" spiffworkflow:operation="delegate_to_local_agent" spiffworkflow:connectorParams="{&#34;agent&#34;: &#34;Connector Agent&#34;, &#34;instruction&#34;: &#34;{{ task_data.instruction }}&#34;}" spiffworkflow:resultVariable="connector_result" spiffworkflow:aiToolParams="{&#34;properties&#34;: {&#34;instruction&#34;: {&#34;type&#34;: &#34;string&#34;, &#34;description&#34;: &#34;A self-contained work order for the connector builder: which provider's API to integrate, what the process needs to call, and the documentation or OpenAPI URL if the work item named one. It cannot see the work item, so repeat anything it needs.&#34;}}, &#34;required&#34;: [&#34;instruction&#34;]}">
        <bpmn:documentation>Hand the job to the Connector Agent, which builds a Processa connector — base URL, auth type and one operation per API method — from a plain-words work order. Use this when the work item asks for an integration with an external API. It writes the connector disabled and reports what a person must still do.</bpmn:documentation>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
    </bpmn:adHocSubProcess>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_orchestrator_agent">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_orchestrator_agent" bpmnElement="orchestrator_agent">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="start_di" bpmnElement="start">
        <dc:Bounds x="160" y="180" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="139" y="223" width="79" height="27" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="read_brief_di" bpmnElement="read_brief">
        <dc:Bounds x="250" y="158" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="orchestrate_di" bpmnElement="orchestrate">
        <dc:Bounds x="380" y="158" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="answer_di" bpmnElement="answer">
        <dc:Bounds x="510" y="158" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="end_di" bpmnElement="end">
        <dc:Bounds x="640" y="180" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="631" y="223" width="55" height="14" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="orchestrator_tools_di" bpmnElement="orchestrator_tools" isExpanded="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="380" y="330" width="550" height="240" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="delegate_connector_agent_di" bpmnElement="delegate_connector_agent">
        <dc:Bounds x="420" y="390" width="200" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f1_di" bpmnElement="f1">
        <di:waypoint x="196" y="198" />
        <di:waypoint x="250" y="198" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f2_di" bpmnElement="f2">
        <di:waypoint x="350" y="198" />
        <di:waypoint x="380" y="198" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f3_di" bpmnElement="f3">
        <di:waypoint x="480" y="198" />
        <di:waypoint x="510" y="198" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f4_di" bpmnElement="f4">
        <di:waypoint x="610" y="198" />
        <di:waypoint x="640" y="198" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
